:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-42" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128606} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-30" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128607} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-72" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128608} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-96" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128609} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-84" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128610}] :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186128605}] :question/math-academy-id "q-72908" :question/problem "Let $R = [2, 5] \\cdot [- 2, 2]$ be a region in the $xy$-plane, and let $f(x, y)$ be a function defined over $R$.\nThe lower and upper Riemann sums corresponding to an arbitrary partition $P$ of $R$ are given by\n\n$L(f, P)|= ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)(2y_{j - 1} - 2x_{i} + 1)Δx_{i}Δy_{j},; U(f, P)|= ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)(2y_{j} - 2x_{i - 1} + 1)Δx_{i}Δy_{j}$.\n\nUsing the definition of the double integral in terms of $L(f, P)$ and $U(f, P)$, compute $∬_(R)f(x, y)dA$.\n\n*Hint: You may wish to make use of the following results:*\n$∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)(x_{i - 1} + x_{i})Δx_{i}Δy_{j} = (x_{m}^{2} - x_{0}^{2})(y_{n} - y_{0}); ∑_(i = 1)^(m)∑_(j = 1)^(n)Δx_{i}Δy_{j} = (x_{m} - x_{0})(y_{n} - y_{0})$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186259571 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "210" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256865} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "162" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186256942} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "234" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257129} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "258" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257852} {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "306" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186257880}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "